# Postgres (docker compose service "db"; the dev server uses its host port 54329).
# Give the dev server its own database (`docker exec inkledger-db createdb -U inkledger inkledger_dev`):
# a production server marks its database, and other processes refuse to migrate it.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://inkledger:change-me@127.0.0.1:54329/inkledger_dev
# docker compose only: the database password (same as in DATABASE_URL)
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
# Required in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-with-a-random-string
# The key trackers' credentials are sealed with (`openssl rand -hex 32`); unset,
# it is derived from SESSION_SECRET. To change it, keep the old one as
# CREDENTIALS_KEY_OLD for one start: every secret is sealed again with the new
# one. Backups hold sealed secrets: restoring one needs the same key.
# CREDENTIALS_KEY=
# CREDENTIALS_KEY_OLD=
# The first admin's password on a new server (changed at the first sign-in)
# INKLEDGER_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Production server port (Docker publishes it on 127.0.0.1:47823)
PORT=47823
# Time zone: inherited from the system; set only to override it
# TZ=Europe/Rome
# Comma-separated host names the server answers to ("*" = any).
# Production default: localhost,127.0.0.1,::1
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Refuse every write to a tracker (1/true/yes): use it for test servers and copied databases
# (JIRA_READ_ONLY=1 is the older name and still works)
# PROVIDERS_READ_ONLY=1
# Days a session lasts when unused (sessions in use are renewed)
# SESSION_DAYS=30
# Minutes between background Jira syncs (0 disables)
# SYNC_INTERVAL_MIN=5
# Module store behind Settings → Store ("off" disables it, the only outbound call besides Jira)
# STORE_URL=off
# Real weather for modules (Open-Meteo, coordinates rounded to 0.1°)
# WEATHER=off
# Comma-separated self-hosted tracker hosts accepted (empty = any); services
# on the internet (Jira Cloud, GitHub) are never limited by it
# REMOTE_ALLOWED_HOSTS=
# Your own GitHub OAuth App (device flow) instead of inkledger's (README → Connecting GitHub)
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# Behind a TLS proxy (e.g. `tailscale serve` for the native apps, docs/native.md):
# TRUST_PROXY=1     # client IP from X-Forwarded-For (login rate limit)
# COOKIE_SECURE=1   # Secure session cookie even without X-Forwarded-Proto
# Let a non-production process migrate a database a production server marked as its own
# ALLOW_MIGRATE_PRODUCTION_DB=1
# Folder for scheduled database backups (Docker: /backups, mounted from the host)
# BACKUP_DIR=
